  "issuedISO": "2026-11-22T09:05:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "A small, medium period northwest swell will level out this morning and then gradually fall through Monday as will responding north and west- facing shore surf. A much larger moderate size, long period north swell will build in Tuesday and this will lift surf along north and west-facing shores to High Surf Advisory levels Tuesday and Wednesday. Gales behind a upstream compact central North Pacific low Tuesday will be directed at the islands. This large size, long period northwest swell will arrive Thanksgiving Day and is expected to push surf to High Surf Warning heights. High surf, along with strong northerly winds behind a cold front, will produce rough sea conditions. This swell will shift more northerly as it subsides Friday through Saturday. Moderate to locally fresh trades will maintain above seasonal average east-facing shore chop through the day. As trades weaken the next few days, as will east shore choppy conditions with a much more tranquil sea state late Monday through Tuesday. Fresh to strong northerly winds and a north swell wrap will likely affect eastern shores Thanksgiving Day and Friday. Other than a very small bump in south swell later this week, there is no significant south energy expected the next several days.",
